{"id":29634,"slug":"defending-your-life","title":"Defending Your Life","year":1991,"country":"United States","duration":111,"spine":1071,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/29634-defending-your-life","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/9b63f522575ce8171a84443e985dbd7b/cSgOmQUCggSN7pk6qfvRhRDKQxUDDZ_large.jpg","description":"Is there love after death? Acerbic everyman Albert Brooks finds a perfect balance between satirical bite and romantic-comedy charm as the writer, director, and star of this wonderfully warm and imaginative existential fantasy. After he dies suddenly, the hapless advertising executive Daniel Miller (Brooks) finds himself in Judgment City, a gleaming way station where the newly deceased must prove they lived a life of sufficient courage to advance in their journey through the universe. As the self-doubting Daniel struggles to make his case, a budding relationship with the uninhibited Julia (Meryl Streep) offers him a chance to finally feel alive. Buoyed by a pitch-perfect supporting cast that includes Rip Torn, Lee Grant, and Buck Henry, Defending Your Life is a rare feat of personal, philosophical filmmaking that happens to also be divinely entertaining.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Albert Brooks","slug":"albert-brooks"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Albert Brooks","role":"Daniel Miller","slug":"albert-brooks"},{"actor":"Meryl Streep","role":"Julia","slug":"meryl-streep"},{"actor":"Rip Torn","role":"Bob Diamond","slug":"rip-torn"},{"actor":"Lee Grant","role":"Lena Foster","slug":"lee-grant"},{"actor":"Buck Henry","role":"Dick Stanley","slug":"buck-henry"},{"actor":"Lillian Lehman","role":"Daniel’s judges","slug":"lillian-lehman"},{"actor":"George Wallace","role":null,"slug":"george-wallace"},{"actor":"Gary Beach","role":"Car salesman","slug":"gary-beach"},{"actor":"Time Winters","role":"Porter","slug":"time-winters"},{"actor":"Mary Pat Gleason","role":"Breakfast waitress","slug":"mary-pat-gleason"},{"actor":"Roger